6:    "changelog": "v2.2 ([REDACTED]03): added capit_margin_lever block ([REDACTED], enabled=false) — margin on the CAPIT bear-washout sleeve only, fixed f=1.3, gate dd52<=-20%, DNSE [REDACTED] package 1840, [REDACTED] only. Wiring + rehearsal complete (job Taylor_20260803_122554, report mike/agents/Taylor/research/margin_kelly_[REDACTED]_wiring_20260803.md); ZERO live behaviour change while enabled=false. Scope is exactly what the p1-p5 research chain verified (p5 engine tier, quant-skeptic [REDACTED]D-medium: dCAGR +0.663pp, dMaxDD worse 0.067pp, DSR 1.0, PBO 0.10-0.14) — NOT the p4 proxy numbers (+1.82pp), which p5 showed inflate both directions. Flipping enabled=true requires a separate explicit user confirmation; no agent may flip it. | v2.1 ([REDACTED]03): added neutral_parking section (governance policy, not a research change) — codifies the engine default that at DT5G NEUTRAL with 0 active BAL/LAG deals, idle cash parks into [REDACTED]V at 70% OF THE IDLE POOL (not a total-equity cap). Reason: go-live [REDACTED] DollarBill wrote target_equity_pct=93.8% straight into a trade plan JSON that passed no policy/backtest gate; user caught it via direct questioning; backtest confirmed 70% is the risk-adjusted optimum. Evidence pinned: jobs Taylor_20260703_113818 (70 vs 94 isolated, quant-skeptic [REDACTED]11:57:15), _120555 (70-100 sweep, no inflection), _130720 (CANONICAL full 2-book NAV: park0.70 CAGR26.83/Sh1.78/DD-16.5/Cal1.63 DOMINATES park0.94 28.01/1.66/-18.8/1.49 and park1.00 29.30/1.65/-19.3/1.52 on Sharpe+Calmar+MaxDD every window), _153738 (70 = properly-tested level, not a taste floor). Added risk_dial_override (PROPOSED/[REDACTED], same guardrail pattern as deep_cheap_recovery_override/v25_leverage): any plan setting NEUTRAL park!=0.70 must carry risk_dial_confirmed_by_user:true + risk_dial_warning_acknowledged citing the job-130720 Sharpe/Calmar/DD cost, else Mafee BLOCKS. No algorithm/backtest logic changed — policy record only. | v2.0 ([REDACTED]29): added gap_adaptive_fill block (PROPOSED, enabled=false) — Layer-3 fill timing becomes gap_z-conditional: abnormal DOWN-gap (gap_z<-2) on a buy-list name -> BUY-AT-OPEN (current rule wrongly waits to 11:15, leaving ~173-206 bps); UP-gap unchanged. Evidence gap_adaptive_proxy.py (daily N=408k IS+OOS) + gap_path_crosscheck.py (16-name 1-min). Pure execution, zero alpha risk; paper-first, LIVE needs user approval. | v1.9 ([REDACTED]27): added v25_leverage block — NAMING V2.5 = V2.4 + leverage (user); account [REDACTED] (DNSE [REDACTED] loan_package_id=1840, borrow 12.5%) user-confirmed; documents B2(breaker-15% DONE)/B3(NAV-cap100B DONE)/B4(PE-freshness DONE) safety gates + risk layering. STATUS=[REDACTED] (prep) — paper until live-recommend integration + final user go-ahead; go-live [REDACTED]30 = V2.4 leverage-free, unaffected. v1.8 ([REDACTED]27): MGE ceiling RAISED 1.30 -> 1.50 per Spyros mge20-tail-review decision (mge20-tail-review-REJECT-cap-at-1.5, [REDACTED]27) — Taylor full 4-point MGE sweep on stable cache showed 1.5 better in-sample (lean default) over 1.3, LUMPY but manageable; 2.0 rejected (tail risk). Episode-drawdown breaker threshold updated -12% -> -15% to match the wider 1.5x ceiling (Spyros: -12% was calibrated for 1.3x; at 1.5x the wider position warrants 3pp more tolerance before knife-catcher fires). Spyros implements in risk_monitor.py (S4 breach = BOT_STOP + Telegram + halt-review flag for first 6m go-live). v1.7 ([REDACTED]26): added macro_kill_switches section (3 RECOVERY_PARK suspend conditions required by Spyros's v24-golive-risk-review sign-off, [REDACTED]23) ahead of go-live [REDACTED]30 — (A) SBV deposit rate >7.5% -> suspend new recovery deploy (outer hard-stop on top of the money_condition throttle); (B) median liquid-universe pb_z > -0.3 while a recovery episode is active -> tighten (stop adding, market no longer cheap; -0.5-in/-0.3-out hysteresis vs deep_cheap_recovery_override episode-open); (C) cumulative intra-episode NAV drawdown > -12% from episode entry -> HALT via BOT_STOP (knife-catching circuit breaker, distinct from the intraday -5% brake). All are SUSPEND (auto-arming, not permanent-off) except (C) which needs human review to restart. v1.6 ([REDACTED]23): deep_cheap_recovery_override ceiling TIGHTENED 1.50 -> 1.30. v1.5 ([REDACTED]23): money_condition dep_floor 0.06->0.075. v1.4 ([REDACTED]22): added money_condition.",
